{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LazySegmentTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10RangeTrees12MonoidActionP","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","text":"MonoidAction"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","t